\f0\fs22 \cf0 Whispers of the Wind is a project, part of a public exhibition 
\f1\i Disruptive Tendencies
\f0\i0 , responding to \'93
\f1\i It\'92s Freezing in LA!\'94
\f0\i0  climate magazine, exploring how a single storm fractures into many personal truths across Ireland. As storms grow stronger and more unpredictable, the project examines the space between meteorological data and lived experience.\
\
This exhibition was created in collaboration with Bulcs\'fa Plette, Mario Onofrei, Hollie Gordon and Kathleen O\'92Kelly.
\f2 \

\f0 \
At the centre of the installation is an embroidered storm chart, where red, orange, and yellow threads trace weather-warning paths along stitched isobars. Visitors draw a tarot-inspired card and follow its colour-coded path, encountering fragments of narrative shaped by myth, memory, and misinformation. A looping mandala-style animation and accompanying booklet further unravel how information bends as it moves through place and people.\
\
Rather than offering certainty, the project lingers in ambiguity, quietly disrupting how climate data is consumed and understood.\
